#: ../../../tabs.md:36
msgid "Vertical Tabs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:39
msgid ""
"Add `:orientation: vertical` to a `tab-set` or `tab-set-code` to stack the "
"labels down a rail on the left (on the right on right-to-left pages), with "
"the selected content beside them. This suits sets holding more labels than "
"fit on one line, where the horizontal layout wraps them into a strip that is "
"hard to scan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:0
msgid "A longer label"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:55
msgid "Content 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:63
msgid ""
"::::{tab-set}\n"
":orientation: vertical\n"
"\n"
":::{tab-item} Label1\n"
"Content 1\n"
":::\n"
"\n"
":::{tab-item} Label2\n"
"Content 2\n"
":::\n"
"\n"
"::::\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:66
msgid ""
".. tab-set::\n"
"    :orientation: vertical\n"
"\n"
"    .. tab-item:: Label1\n"
"\n"
"        Content 1\n"
"\n"
"    .. tab-item:: Label2\n"
"\n"
"        Content 2\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:72
msgid ""
"The rail is as wide as its longest label, up to 35% of the set; a longer "
"label wraps at its spaces. Below the `md` breakpoint (a viewport 768px wide) "
"the set falls back to the horizontal layout, two columns being too narrow to "
"read at that width. The breakpoint follows the viewport, not the set's "
"container, so a vertical set in a narrow column (a grid cell, say) stays "
"vertical on a wide screen. Themes that restyle the tab labels themselves, "
"such as pydata-sphinx-theme and sphinx-book-theme, may draw them less neatly "
"in the rail until they style `sd-tab-set-vertical` too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:77
msgid "Synchronised Tabs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:79
msgid ""
"The Selection of tab items can be synchronised across multiple tab-sets. For "
"a `tab-item` to be synchronisable, add the `sync` option to the `tab-item` "
"directive with a key unique to that set. Now when you select a tab in one "
"set, tabs in other sets with the same key will be selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:84
msgid "Synchronisation requires that JavaScript is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:88
msgid ""
"To synchronise tabs only across certain tab-sets, add the `:sync-group:` "
"option to each `tab-set` directive with the same group name, such as `:sync-"
"group: category`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:90
msgid ""
"You can also add an [HTML query string](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Query_string) to the end of the page's URL, to automatically select a tab "
"with a specific key across all tab-sets of the group, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:93
msgid ""
"[`?category=key1#synchronised-tabs`](?category=key1#synchronised-tabs)"
"{.external}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:94
msgid ""
"[`?category=key2#synchronised-tabs`](?category=key2#synchronised-tabs)"
"{.external}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:134
msgid ""
"::::{tab-set}\n"
":sync-group: category\n"
"\n"
":::{tab-item} Label1\n"
":sync: key1\n"
"\n"
"Content 1\n"
":::\n"
"\n"
":::{tab-item} Label2\n"
":sync: key2\n"
"\n"
"Content 2\n"
":::\n"
"\n"
"::::\n"
"\n"
"::::{tab-set}\n"
":sync-group: category\n"
"\n"
":::{tab-item} Label1\n"
":sync: key1\n"
"\n"
"Content 1\n"
":::\n"
"\n"
":::{tab-item} Label2\n"
":sync: key2\n"
"\n"
"Content 2\n"
":::\n"
"\n"
"::::\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:137
msgid ""
".. tab-set::\n"
"    :sync-group: category\n"
"\n"
"    .. tab-item:: Label1\n"
"        :sync: key1\n"
"\n"
"        Content 1\n"
"\n"
"    .. tab-item:: Label2\n"
"        :sync: key2\n"
"\n"
"        Content 2\n"
"\n"
".. tab-set::\n"
"    :sync-group: category\n"
"\n"
"    .. tab-item:: Label1\n"
"        :sync: key1\n"
"\n"
"        Content 1\n"
"\n"
"    .. tab-item:: Label2\n"
