"\n"
"        Content 2\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:143
msgid "Linking to synchronised tabs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:145
msgid ""
"To author a link that pre-selects a tab, append the query string (and "
"optionally a page anchor) to the URL of the **built** HTML page. Sphinx "
"referencing roles, such as `ref` and `doc`, cannot output URLs containing "
"query strings, so instead write the URL directly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:149
msgid ""
"In MyST Markdown, add an `external` class to the link (using the "
"[`attrs_inline` extension](https://myst-parser.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"
"syntax/optional.html)), so that the URL is output as-is, rather than being "
"resolved as a cross-reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:150
msgid "In reStructuredText, use a standard (external) hyperlink."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:153
msgid ""
"[Open with key2 selected](tabs.html?category=key2#synchronised-tabs)"
"{.external}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:156
msgid "`Open with key2 selected <tabs.html?category=key2#synchronised-tabs>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:161
msgid ""
"For example: [open the tabs above with `key2` selected](tabs.html?"
"category=key2#synchronised-tabs){.external}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:164
msgid ""
"Such URLs are relative to the location of the current page in the built HTML "
"output, not to the source files (for example, a page in a sub-folder would "
"require `../tabs.html?...`). They are not checked by Sphinx, so they will "
"break silently if the target page is moved, and they do not apply to other "
"output formats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:170
msgid "Tabbed code examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:172
msgid ""
"The `tab-set-code` directive provides a shorthand for synced code examples. "
"You can place any directives in a `tab-set-code` that produce a "
"`literal_block` node with a `language` attribute, for example `code`, `code-"
"block` and `literalinclude`. Tabs will be labelled and synchronised by the "
"`language` attribute (in upper-case)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:177
msgid ""
"You can also add an [HTML query string](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Query_string) to the end of the page's URL, to automatically select a tab "
"with a specific code across all tab-sets of the group, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:180
msgid ""
"[`?code=markdown#tabbed-code-examples`](?code=markdown#tabbed-code-examples)"
"{.external}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tabs.md:181
msgid ""
"[`?code=rst#tabbed-code-examples`](?code=rst#tabbed-code-examples){.external}"
msgstr ""

